{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fruity-conclusive-goral","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nReconciler unit-test cases and fixtures under `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/`. contains confirmed comment or docstring bloat from the audit pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`. The file-specific constraints must survive consolidation.\n\n## Approach\nDelegate remediation to bounded directory/subsystem leaf cohorts. Each leaf edits only its declared paths, preserves the requirements recorded in its Scope, and supplies the authoritative file-impact set. This keeps responsibilities non-overlapping and each change reviewable in one session.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every migrated path in this workstream appears in exactly one leaf Scope and matching file-impact record; verified by the migration inventory.\n- [ ] Each path's comments or docstrings retain its listed current constraints and consumer contract while removing redundant text; verified by the leaf's row-by-row completion comment.\n- [ ] Each leaf's declared verification commands exit 0 before that leaf closes.\n\n## Child decomposition\nEach directory/subsystem cohort owns all three criteria for its exact path set. Cohort path sets are disjoint; their union is this workstream's scope.","id":"bea4-b9cc-18cc-40c4","parent_id":"3e32-a859-2153-4a1b","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Condense reconciler unit-test comments"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788570329844470113,"uuid":"e4a3337f-17fd-464e-b37e-8cd489242741"}